	.TITLE	IFC$RTL_MACRO - IFC run-time wrappers in MACRO-32
	.IDENT	/X01.00-01/
;
; MACRO-32 replacement for IFCRTL_BLISS.BLI, for systems without BLISS
; (x86-64 by default; see [.IFC]DESCRIP.MMS).  It uses the .CALL_ENTRY
; directive of the MACRO-32 compiler, so it is for Alpha, I64 and x86-64,
; not VAX MACRO.
;
; Edit History:
; 31-Oct-2026  Added for builds on OpenVMS x86-64 V9.2-3 without BLISS.
;
; IFC$MESSAGE and IFC$MESSAGE_INDENT are called from Pascal with a variable
; length argument list.  Each one passes the address of its own argument
; list (VAX format: a longword count followed by longword arguments) to the
; Pascal routine that does the work.
;
; HOME_ARGS=TRUE makes the MACRO-32 compiler build that VAX-style argument
; list in memory, so AP can be passed as its address.
;
	.PSECT	$CODE$, PIC, CON, REL, LCL, SHR, EXE, RD, NOWRT, QUAD

IFC$MESSAGE::
	.CALL_ENTRY	MAX_ARGS=255, HOME_ARGS=TRUE
	PUSHL	AP
	CALLS	#1, G^IFC$MESSAGE_LIST
	RET

IFC$MESSAGE_INDENT::
	.CALL_ENTRY	MAX_ARGS=255, HOME_ARGS=TRUE
	PUSHL	AP
	CALLS	#1, G^IFC$MESSAGE_INDENT_LIST
	RET

	.END
